<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal sets conditions on Tabaqueira sale.</title>
<headline>Portugal sets conditions on Tabaqueira sale.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Portuguese government set the following conditions on the sale of a 65 percent stake in state-owned tobacco firm Tabaqueira to a consortium led by U.S. firm Philip Morris.</p>
<p>- The consortium must sell all wholesale businesses held directly or indirectly by Tabaqueira as soon as possible and within a year.</p>
<p>- The consortium must not force any retailer to stock its products exclusively.</p>
<p>The consortium, which is 80 percent owned by Philip Morris and 20 percent by Portugal's Mello group, will pay some 33 billion escudos ($210 million) for the stake.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
